   "body": "**Adversarial review (Claude Fable 5.1, ext/bybifok-fable-review-10, independent of the author): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 81f42900\n\n1. **High** — `JSONTokenizer.swift:119,139`, `JSONWriter.swift:12`, `JSONWriterTests.swift:13`, `MPStoragePageParserTests.swift:92`: five `String(decoding:as: UTF8.self)`. `optional_data_string_conversion` is a default rule (confirmed on its docs page; base already disables it in `TextDecoding.swift:40`), CI runs `swiftlint --strict` over Tests too → the SwiftLint job goes red on this head. Fix: `String(validating:)` or a `swiftlint:disable:this`. Note: `1fe51c9e`, pushed after this head, does exactly that; the verdict is for 81f42900. On that newer head, `JSONWriter.write`'s `?? \"\"` is a silent empty document if ever reached — prefer a throw/precondition.\n2. **Low** — `JSONTreeDecoder.swift:83`: a non-zero lexeme rounding to zero (`1e-400` Double, `1e-50` Float) decodes 0, where `JSONDecoder` throws (probed on macOS 27; same guard in swift-foundation 6.2). Spec §2 claims Foundation's conversions; the 17 samples miss it. No modelled field decodes Double, so no document changes. Add the samples (they fail today) and either refuse or list under \"Intentional differences\".\n3. **Low** — `JSONTreeDecoder.swift:54-89`: `null` for a scalar is `typeMismatch`; Foundation gives `valueNotFound`. Nothing in HFRModels tells them apart; state it in the spec.\n4. **Nit** — spec §3 \"encodes nothing → `{}`\" is tested only at the top; writing `null` nested (`JSONTreeEncoder.swift:118,160`) passes every suite.\n5. **Nit** — `maximumDepth = 512`: at 1000 the depth test dies SIGBUS on the 512 KiB debug test thread; comment that the thread stack, not only parity, bounds it.\n\n**Checked**: build + 1221 tests (5 bundles) green; 16 mutations, 15 caught (every spec claim); grammar, first-duplicate, 512/513, UTF-8 key order, lowercase escapes verified against swift-foundation swift-6.2-RELEASE sources (Linux CI) and a macOS probe; public API of `JSONValue`/`JSONNumber`/`MPStorageCodec` unchanged; no network/cookie surface, pure HFRModels, Foundation-free tokenizer/writer; Swift 6 (coders local, `JSONValue` Sendable); lines ≤140, complexity ≤10 (`append`=10, limit `>10`), identifiers, nesting, `private(set)` in private struct OK, whitespace; legacy `MPStorage.m:884-886/908-909` verified; HFR-PROTOCOL R60a claim backed by `writtenAsBefore` on the capture; LOT-062 updated, LOTS.md untouched (EXTERNAL-AGENTS); `Closes #97`/`Claim:` match the issue's `/claim`; LESSONS 1-4, 12, 16, 17, 21, 22, 31, 53. Scratch worktree removed; /Users/yendi/Dev/HFRnow-wt-073 untouched.\n",
