   "body": "**Adversarial review (Claude Fable 5.1, ext/bybifok-fable-review-10, independent of the author): APPROVE** — head 167e2a5d\n\nNo findings that block. Residual notes:\n\n1. **Nit** — `JSONTreeDecoder.swift:97-100` (`isNonZero`): `Character` range comparison on the lexeme; fine since the lexeme is validated ASCII, but a comment saying so would stop a future `Unicode`-aware reading. No action needed.\n2. **Nit** — the merge `5905d329` brought LOT-035/LOT-091 into this branch; the PR diff against `dev-swift` stays the 17 LOT-073 files. Squash-merge as usual.\n\n**Checked** (fresh worktree at 167e2a5d, removed after):\n- `swift build --build-tests` green, no warnings in MPStorage/JSON files; `swift test --skip-build`: 1252 tests in 5 bundles green.\n- Mutations, 10/10 caught: Double accepting a rounded-to-zero number; Int refusing `1e-400`; `null` as `typeMismatch` for scalars/containers; Bool-null as `valueNotFound`; nested nothing written `null`; `/` escaped; keys sorted as Swift strings; uppercase hex; every zero treated as rounded (`-0`, `0e-400`); controls unescaped.\n- Linux parity, swift-foundation swift-6.2-RELEASE sources: integer slow path has no rounding-to-zero guard (`1e-400` → 0), only `unwrapFloatingPoint` has `isTrueZero`; Bool decode goes straight to type mismatch in single, keyed and unkeyed containers; `checkNotNull`/`valueNotFound` for strings, integers, floats, keyed and unkeyed containers. macOS 27 probe agrees, including `10e-400`, `-0e5`, `0.000e-999`, `[Bool]`/`[null]` (`Index 0` path) and `{\"inner\":{},\"list\":[{}]}`.\n- High follow-up: no `String(decoding:)` or `?? \"\"` left; the writer appends scalars, no normalization (bytes equal `JSONEncoder`'s in `escapes`, `keyOrder`, `nested`, R60a `writtenAsBefore`).\n- Merge resolution: vs 8c59262f only the PR's 17 files differ, vs 1fe51c9e only dev-swift's; no markers; HFR-PROTOCOL §6c has LOT-035 then LOT-073.\n- Lint: lines ≤ 140, no trailing/double blank lines, complexity ≤ 10, nesting, identifiers; spec matches code (21 × 10 matrix, new \"shown to fail\" rows).\n- Fork head re-checked: `lot/073-json-tokenizer` = 167e2a5d. `Closes #97` / `Claim:` unchanged. Original worktree untouched; nothing posted.\n",
